{"verdict":"changes_requested","summary":"The diff contains zero source code changes — only .epam/codeline-facts.json and .epam/settings.json were added. The prescribed root-cause fix was not implemented at all. src/services/contentstack.ts has no live_preview config in the Stack options (confirmed by reading the file — the options object at line 55 has api_key, delivery_token, environment, branch, fetchOptions but no live_preview). src/context/contentstackContext.tsx remains a bare createContext<IContentstackContext>({}) with no Provider component, no useState, no useEffect, and no live preview event subscription. src/hooks/useContent.ts calls useContext on a static context with no reactive update path. No vitest unit tests exist — test/unit/ directory has zero files. A search for live_preview, onEntryChange, onLiveUpdate, live-preview-utils, LivePreview, and CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW across the entire project returned zero matches. All four verification criteria are unmet.","issues":[{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/services/contentstack.ts","line":55,"description":"The options object passed to contentstack.Stack(options) does NOT include a live_preview configuration block. The prescribed root-cause fix requires adding live_preview: { enable: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_ENABLE === 'true', preview_token: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN, host: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST } (conditionally spread, like fetchOptions is today). Without this, the Contentstack SDK never processes live preview data — every downstream consumer (useContent, ContentstackProvider, 236+ components) is starved of preview content. This is the root cause identified in the RCA and it remains completely unaddressed. No changes were made to this file at all — confirmed by reading the file: the options object contains api_key, delivery_token, environment, branch, and fetchOptions only.","suggestedFix":"Add CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_ENABLE, CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN, and CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST to the process.env destructuring block. Then add a conditionally-spread live_preview property to the options object: ...(CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_ENABLE === 'true' ? { live_preview: { enable: true, preview_token: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN, host: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST } } : {}). Use preview_token, NOT management_token."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/context/contentstackContext.tsx","line":18,"description":"The file exports a bare createContext<IContentstackContext>({}) with NO Provider component, NO useState, NO useEffect, and NO onEntryChange/onLivePreview subscription. The prescribed client-side fix requires a ContentstackProvider component that uses useState(defaultContent) as the content source and a useEffect that subscribes to Contentstack live preview events (Stack.onLivePreview or window message listener per Contentstack SDK docs) and calls setContent with merged preview data. Without a reactive Provider, useContent (consumed by 236+ components) always returns the static SSR-provided default content. No real-time preview updates can ever reach any consumer. All acceptance criteria related to real-time/draft content display are unmet. Confirmed by reading the file — it is 25 lines, exports only ContentstackContext, no Provider."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/hooks/useContent.ts","line":5,"description":"useContent calls useContext(ContentstackContext) but there is no reactive Provider component supplying a changing value. The hook will always return the static value passed at render time. Even if Contentstack live preview events fired, there is no state setter to trigger re-renders of the 236+ consumers. The hook cannot propagate live preview updates as-is. This is a consequence of the missing ContentstackProvider (blocker above). Confirmed by reading the file — it uses useContext(ContentstackContext) with no reactive source."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"test/unit/","line":0,"description":"No vitest unit tests exist for the Live Preview feature. The test/unit/ directory does not exist at all (confirmed via list_files — zero files returned). Review criteria require new features to have corresponding vitest unit tests mirroring the src/ path. At minimum, tests should verify: (1) Stack options include a live_preview block with enable=true and preview_token when CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_ENABLE is 'true', (2) ContentstackProvider re-renders consumers when a live preview event fires, (3) content state merges incoming preview data correctly, (4) the page renders without errors when preview provides invalid/errored content. I searched for test/unit/**/* via list_files and found zero files. I searched src/ for onEntryChange|onLiveUpdate|live-preview-utils|live_preview|LivePreview and found zero matches.","suggestedFix":"Create test/unit/context/contentstackContext.test.tsx and test/unit/services/contentstack.test.ts with vitest tests covering: Stack options live_preview config, ContentstackProvider reactive state updates on preview events, multi-field updates, and graceful handling of invalid/errored preview content."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/interface/contentstack.ts","line":0,"description":"ICreateQueryConfig, ICreateEntryConfig, and ICommonContentstackConfig interfaces were not updated with an optional live_preview parameter. The prescribed fix requires adding an optional live_preview field so that live preview hash data can flow through to Contentstack queries. Without it, queries will always return published content even if the Stack is configured for live preview. No changes were made to this file. Confirmed by searching src/interface for live_preview|ICreateQueryConfig|ICreateEntryConfig|ICommonContentstackConfig — zero matches for live_preview.","suggestedFix":"Add an optional live_preview field to ICreateQueryConfig and ICreateEntryConfig interfaces, and forward it through createContentTypeQuery/createContentTypeEntryQuery to the Contentstack query chain (e.g., query.includeFallback() or passing live_preview hash context)."},{"severity":"major","file":"package.json","line":0,"description":"The @contentstack/live-preview-utils dependency is not installed anywhere in the project. A search for 'live-preview-utils' across the entire project returned zero matches. Without this SDK, no client-side Live Preview subscription can be established, making real-time content updates impossible. Note: the RCA mentions Stack.onLivePreview or window message listener — verify whether the contentstack delivery SDK already provides this or whether live-preview-utils is required.","suggestedFix":"Install @contentstack/live-preview-utils if the Contentstack delivery SDK's built-in live preview events are insufficient. Import and initialize it in ContentstackProvider's useEffect to subscribe to entry change events."},{"severity":"major","file":"src/services/contentstack.ts","line":69,"description":"getStaticProps in page components does not forward context.preview or context.previewData (or a live_preview URL param) to Contentstack service calls. No pages/api/preview.ts route exists to enable Next.js draft mode (confirmed via list_files — no files matching src/pages/api/preview* found). Even if the service layer supported live_preview, draft content would never be fetched because the page-level code doesn't pass preview context through. While the RCA focuses on the Stack options and Provider, without forwarding preview context through the query chain, the server-side rendering path will always return published content.","suggestedFix":"Add a pages/api/preview.ts route to enable Next.js draft mode, and forward context.preview/live_preview hash from getStaticProps to Contentstack service calls so draft content is fetched server-side during preview sessions."}]}
